description:
At Broadridge, we've built a culture where the highest goal is to empower others to accomplish more. If you’re passionate about developing your career, while helping others along the way, come join the Broadridge team.




**Role Overview**
 The QA Engineer is a quality\-focused individual with solid technical expertise in testing and validating trading platform solutions for our clients. In this role, you will ensure the quality and reliability of Broadridge trading systems for high\-touch and low\-touch Agency trading desks through comprehensive testing strategies, within the context of client delivery projects. This position will lead to a deeper understanding of international financial markets and to an excellent knowledge of our product suite.




 Within the Professional Services department, you will drive quality assurance across client platform implementations following the Agile methodology.




**Responsibilities**
* Work with project managers, client product specialists, implementation engineers, technical architects, and technical leads in squads to define and execute testing strategies, and report on quality metrics and testing progress to clients and internal stakeholders;
* Work with our clients to analyse their requirements and issues from a business, functional, and technical perspective to design appropriate test plans and test cases;
* Assist project managers in estimating and sizing QA effort within project timelines;
* Design, develop, and execute functional, regression, integration, and performance test cases for trading platform configurations and customizations;
* Identify, document, and track defects through their full lifecycle, collaborating with implementation engineers, client teams and customer support teams for timely resolution;
* Build and maintain automated test scripts and frameworks to support continuous testing practices across delivery pipelines;
* Provide quality status reporting and sign\-off recommendations to stakeholders ahead of go\-live milestones and production deployments;
* Liaise with our client’s product team, Engineering, and our Technical Account Managers to align on quality standards and coverage expectations;
* Proactively improve testing processes to promote better quality and safer deployments;
* Enhance your business and technical knowledge of international financial markets relating to principal and agency trading, equities and derivatives, FX, and fixed income asset classes; and develop your understanding of Broadridge products which serve these businesses;
* Champion a test\-driven methodology across the delivery team.


**Your profile**
* University degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Science, or equivalent;
* Experience in the finance industry is a must have, such as in high\-touch and low\-touch agency trading systems, market connectivity, and/or asset classes such as equities, derivatives, structured products, FX, and fixed income;
* 2\-5 years of experience in QA, testing, or related roles;
* Strong knowledge of software testing methodologies, including test planning, test case design, and defect lifecycle management;
* Experience with test automation frameworks (e.g. Selenium, pytest, or equivalent);
* FIX and other exchange protocol knowledge is a must have;
* Source control systems (Git);
* Programming experience is a plus;
* Experience in a client\-facing technical support role or an implementation/delivery role;
* Excellent communication skills, including fluent written and oral English;
* Autonomy, organization, and a strong sense of accountability;
* Strong analytical and problem\-solving skills.


 We are dedicated to fostering a collaborative, engaging, and inclusive environment and are committed to providing a workplace that empowers associates to be authentic and bring their best to work. We believe that associates do their best when they feel safe, understood, and valued, and we work diligently and collaboratively to ensure Broadridge is a company—and ultimately a community—that recognizes and celebrates everyone’s unique perspective.




**Use of AI in Hiring**
 As part of the recruiting process, Broadridge may use technology, including artificial intelligence (AI)\-based tools, to help review and evaluate applications. These tools are used only to support our recruiters and hiring managers, and all employment decisions include human review to ensure fairness, accuracy, and compliance with applicable laws. Please note that honesty and transparency are critical to our hiring process. Any attempt to falsify, misrepresent, or disguise information in an application, resume, assessment, or interview will result in disqualification from consideration.
